.TH DB-STORAGE 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
db-storage \- read-only MariaDB/MySQL table storage snapshot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B db-storage
.B --engine
mariadb|mysql
.B --database
NAME
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B db-storage --help
|
.B --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
One bounded, fixed, read-only INFORMATION_SCHEMA.TABLES query reports a TOTAL
for visible base tables in one selected database, plus top-N individual
TABLE records. PostgreSQL and Oracle are not implemented in M5.4.
The metadata is not a filesystem allocation or growth measurement.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --engine mariadb|mysql
Native backend. Required.
.TP
.B --database NAME
Explicit database to inspect. Required. Only simple identifiers supported.
.TP
.B --host HOST, --port PORT, --user NAME
Explicit connection options. TCP requires verifiable TLS.
.TP
.B --timeout 1..30
Native connection timeout, in seconds. Default 5.
.TP
.B --client ABSOLUTE_PATH
Explicit native client executable; otherwise search fixed install locations.
.TP
.B --defaults-file ABSOLUTE_PATH
Private mode-0600 native client credentials/TLS file, with only allowed
[client] options and no symlinks or file includes.
.TP
.B --limit 1..100
Number of top tables to display, default 20. TOTAL always covers all visible
base tables independently of this display limit.
.TP
.B --sort-by total|data|index|free
Sort TABLE records by the named metadata measure, default total.
.TP
.B --null
Emit eleven NUL-separated fields per record (no human headers).
.SH OUTPUT
ENGINE, SCOPE, KIND, NAME, STORAGE_ENGINE, TABLES, DATA_BYTES, INDEX_BYTES,
TOTAL_BYTES, FREE_BYTES, UNKNOWN. KIND is TOTAL or TABLE; SCOPE is visible.
UNKNOWN counts tables where a source size field was NULL.
Sums substitute zero for NULL but return exit status 1 for incomplete metadata.
InnoDB figures can be estimates, and DATA_FREE can be shared tablespace space.
Do not interpret these as filesystem usage or as time-series growth.
.SH PRIVILEGES
The connected role needs rights exposing metadata for the selected database.
A user with only USAGE may see no tables or be unable to select a database;
for a disposable test schema, a privileged administrator can grant SELECT
on only that schema. Neither root nor SQL admin access is used by this command.
.SH SECURITY
No arbitrary SQL, DDL, ANALYZE TABLE, shell command or password argv is
accepted. Local sockets are explicit. On TCP, verified TLS identity is required.
Client output is bounded and validated before any formatted results are printed.
Raw client stderr is never forwarded.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 valid snapshot (including zero visible tables); 1 database error or
NULL metrics; 2 invalid options or unsupported engine; 3 missing native
client, timeout, malformed output or exceeded output limit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
./bin/db-storage --engine mariadb --database sasd_storage_lab \\
  --defaults-file "$HOME/.config/sasd/mysql-probe.cnf" \\
  --sort-by total --limit 10
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR db-probe (1),
.BR db-health (1),
.BR db-activity (1)
